  "query_preview": "..A progressive weather pattern across the Pacific\nand CONUS through early next week keeps the storm track to our\nnorth with a couple upper level trofs moving through the state.\nThe 1st trof moves thru on Saturday bringing a small chance \n(<15%) of snow showers to the White mountains in the morning \nwith the 2nd trof moving through on Monday being dry. Both\nsystems will bring afternoon breezes today and Monday. With \nthis progressive pattern, high temperatures will be on a roller\ncoaster ride thru early next week. The passage of the 1st trof \non Saturday brings in a drier, cooler air mass with overnight \nlows Sunday morning near freezing across some of the eastern \nvalleys. Upper ridging moves across the area in the Tue/Wed time\nframe. Some uncertainty exists for Thanksgiving day if another \ndry trof passes through or will upper ridging holds.\n\n8-14 day outlooks (Fri Nov 27 to Thu Dec 3)\nTemperature: Leaning above normal (40% east to 52% west)\nPrecipitation: Near normal.",
